{"name":"Alligator Gladiator","hex":"#444411","fetched":"2026-10-20","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alligator","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Either of two species of large amphibious reptile, Alligator mississippiensis or Alligator sinensis, in the genus Alligator within order Crocodilia, which have sharp teeth and very strong jaws and are native to the Americas and China, respectively.","A crocodilian of the subfamily Alligatorinae."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To crack in a pattern resembling an alligator's skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alligator"},{"term":"gladiator","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person (professional or slave) who entertained the public by engaging in mortal combat with another, or with a wild animal.","A disputant in a public controversy or debate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fight as entertainment for others.","To compete in a public contest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gladiator"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alligator","blocks":[{"text":"An alligator, or colloquially gator, is a large reptile in the genus Alligator of the family Alligatoridae in the order Crocodilia. The two extant species are the American alligator and the Chinese alligator. Additionally, several extinct species of alligator are known from fossil remains. Alligators first appeared during the late Eocene epoch about 37 million years ago."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Chinese%2Bamerican_alligators.png/330px-Chinese%2Bamerican_alligators.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alligator","wikidata":"Q530397"},{"title":"Gladiator","blocks":[{"text":"A gladiator was an armed combatant who entertained audiences in the Roman Republic and Roman Empire in violent confrontations with other gladiators, wild animals, and condemned criminals. Some gladiators were volunteers who risked their lives and their legal and social standing by appearing in the arena. Most were despised as slaves, schooled under harsh conditions, socially marginalized, and segregated even in death."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Gladiators_from_the_Zliten_mosaic_3.JPG/330px-Gladiators_from_the_Zliten_mosaic_3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gladiator","wikidata":"Q482999"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Chinese%2Bamerican_alligators.png/500px-Chinese%2Bamerican_alligators.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Chinese%2Bamerican_alligators.png/500px-Chinese%2Bamerican_alligators.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChinese%2Bamerican_alligators.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/AmericanAlligator.JPG/500px-AmericanAlligator.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/AmericanAlligator.JPG/1280px-AmericanAlligator.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/AmericanAlligator.JPG/500px-AmericanAlligator.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmericanAlligator.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/ChineseAlligator.jpg/500px-ChineseAlligator.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/ChineseAlligator.jpg/1280px-ChineseAlligator.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content